ElderRobot: DLQ Management API Specification
This document outlines the API endpoints, request/response payloads, and error handling mechanisms required to power the Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) operator dashboard and manage quarantined telemetry records.
1. List Quarantined Payloads
Retrieves a paginated list of failed telemetry records currently sitting in the local SQLite WAL DLQ.
Endpoint: GET /api/v1/dlq/records
Query Parameters:
page (int, default: 1)
limit (int, default: 50)
robot_id (string, optional) - Filter by a specific robot.
error_type (string, optional) - Filter by error category (e.g., ValidationError, AuthError).
Response Body (200 OK):
{
  "total": 3,
  "page": 1,
  "limit": 50,
  "records": [
    {
      "id": "uuid-string-1234",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-10T14:22:01Z",
      "robot_id": "forklift-04",
      "error_type": "ValidationError",
      "error_message": "Field 'battery_level' missing from payload",
      "retry_count": 3,
      "raw_payload": {"robot_id": "forklift-04", "status": "active"}
    }
  ]
}
2. Reprocess Payload
Forces the bridge to take a quarantined record, re-validate it, and push it back into the active cloud sync queue.
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/dlq/reprocess/{id}
Response Body (200 OK):
{
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Record uuid-string-1234 successfully re-injected into sync queue",
  "record_id": "uuid-string-1234"
}
Error Response (404 Not Found): Record ID does not exist in the DLQ.
3. Discard Payload
Permanently purges an unrecoverable or junk record from local storage and logs an audit trail entry.
Endpoint: DELETE /api/v1/dlq/discard/{id}
Response Body (200 OK):
{
  "status": "purged",
  "message": "Record uuid-string-1234 permanently deleted from DLQ",
  "audit_logged": true
}
4. Batch Operations
Allows operators to perform bulk reprocess or bulk discard actions on multiple selected records simultaneously.
Endpoint: POST /api/v1/dlq/batch
Request Body:
{
  "action": "reprocess", 
  "record_ids": ["uuid-1", "uuid-2", "uuid-3"]
}
Response Body (200 OK):
{
  "action": "reprocess",
  "processed_count": 3,
  "failed_count": 0,
  "details": []
}
